 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Durand et al. [4] and Belcour et al. [5, 6] as a framework for frequency analysis of light transport [S1]. It extends the work of Wang et al. [3] on point-based light transport in participating media with refractive boundaries [S1]. The authors implemented the algorithm in the Mitsuba Renderer [14] and compared it against Wang et al. [3], Holzschuch [2], and Unified Points, Beams and Paths (UPBP) by Křivánek et al. [16] [S1].
+The underlying frequency analysis framework was introduced by Durand et al. [4], with the covariance matrix approximation by Belcour et al. [5, 6] [S1]. This specific method extends Wang et al. [3] for point-based light transport in participating media with refractive boundaries [S1]. The authors implemented the algorithm in the Mitsuba Renderer [14] and compared it against Wang et al. [3], Holzschuch [2], and Unified Points, Beams and Paths (UPBP) by Křivánek et al. [16] [S1].
 
